## 4. File Change Summary Tables

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/apps/AppIcon.vue` | Modify | `<template>` `MenubarContent` | Added a URL navigator block (globe-prefixed address input + Go button), rendered only when `hasUrl`, with `@click.stop`/`@keydown.stop` so the menu doesn't hijack typing. |
| `src/components/apps/AppIcon.vue` | Modify | `data()` | Added `urlValue` holding the editable address. |
| `src/components/apps/AppIcon.vue` | Modify | `computed` | Added `appUrl` (`liveApp.params.lastUrl \|\| app.path`) and `hasUrl` (`!!appUrl`). |
| `src/components/apps/AppIcon.vue` | Modify | `watch` | Added an `appUrl` watcher (immediate) to seed/sync the input with the app's real URL. |
| `src/components/apps/AppIcon.vue` | Modify | `methods` | Added `openUrl` (writes `lastUrl` via `$ui.updateAppParams`), `syncUrl` (Esc reset) and `normalizeUrl` (adds `https://` to bare hosts, keeps relative paths). |
| `src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue` | Modify | `computed.tabId` | Also resolves `params.params.app.tabId` so `workspace` panels (which store the app under `params.app`) resolve correctly. |
| `src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue` | Modify | `computed.liveApp` | New computed reading the live store app (`openApps[tabId]`) for reactive param access. |
| `src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue` | Modify | `watch` | New watcher on `liveApp.params.lastUrl` that sets `currentUrl`, forcing the iframe to navigate to the URL typed in the navigator. |

### Accessibility notes
- The input has an explicit `aria-label="App URL"` and `inputmode="url"`.
- The Go button has both `title` and `aria-label`, and is disabled when empty (`:disabled="!urlValue"`).
- Focus ring stays visible (`input-bordered` + daisyUI focus styles); no `outline-none` override on the input.
- `Enter` submits, `Esc` reverts — standard address-bar semantics.

### Anti-patterns avoided
- ❌ Placing the input inside a `MenubarItem` (would select the item and close the menu) — used a plain `div` with propagation stopped.
- ❌ Making the app menu icon the only affordance for a URL change without a live navigation path — `AppWindow` now reacts, keeping the control honest.
- ❌ Inventing a new store action / state — reused `updateAppParams`, the same channel `persistUrl` already uses.

